{
  "_comment": [
    "Scripted flight-data scenarios for the fake provider.",
    "",
    "These are vendor-NEUTRAL: they describe flights in the shape of RawFlight,",
    "not in any provider's JSON. That is what lets them survive a change of",
    "provider, and what lets the frontend be developed against them.",
    "",
    "Times are ISO 8601 with an explicit UTC offset. There is no such thing as",
    "a local time in this file.",
    "",
    "A scenario with no 'flights' key and an 'error' key makes the provider",
    "raise, so the failure paths above it can be exercised on demand.",
    "",
    "A date of '*' matches any date, which keeps demos from going stale."
  ],

